# Gitignored paths carried into every new worktree. Consumed by:
#   - Orca — this is its native, repo-root config file
#   - worktrunk's `wt step copy-ignored`, wired into [post-start] in
#     home/dot_config/worktrunk/config.toml
# Both read this as literal paths (Orca silently drops globs/negation) —
# keep entries literal, one per line.
#
# A subset of the AI-agent state home/bin/wt-sync-agent-files keeps converged
# between existing worktrees (see wt-sync-all): only the entries that are
# actually gitignored here, since Orca skips anything else. CLAUDE.md and
# AGENTS.md aren't listed for the same reason -- they're tracked in git, so
# every worktree already has them.

.omc
.agents/
.agent/
.handoffs/
.serena/
.claude/settings.local.json
